

--> What is JPA?
    JPA (Java Persistence API) is a specification (rules only).
        It defines:
        Annotations
        Interfaces
        Entity lifecycle
        ❌ JPA does NOT provide implementation.

--> Hibernate as JPA Implementation
        Hibernate is the most popular JPA implementation.
        Spring Boot uses Hibernate by default.
        Entity:
        Hibernate

--> Configure Spring Boot with JPA & Hibernate

    spring.datasource.url=jdbc:mysql://localhost:3306/testdb
    spring.datasource.username=root
    spring.datasource.password=admin

    spring.jpa.hibernate.ddl-auto=update
    spring.jpa.show-sql=true
    spring.jpa.properties.hibernate.dialect=org.hibernate.dialect.MySQL8Dialect


--> Hibernate Auto DDL Generation

    | Value    | Meaning                 |
    | -------- | ----------------------- |
    | create   | Drops & creates tables  |
    | update   | Updates existing tables |
    | validate | Validates schema        |
    | none     | No action               |



